==Enemy==
At first sight he may seem like a stronger Traitless [[Mooth]]. Similar range to Mooth too, at 344. While decently fast, his pushing power is not impressive on its own and usually needs the support of stronger frontline units, in which his role becomes apparent in creating openings for them. He also has high health and damage, along with a 100% chance to [[Knockback]] all Cat Units. Any Cat below 350 range is almost guaranteed to be pushed back repeatedly until death do them part. This becomes a larger nuisance when he's accompanied by enemies with [[Omni Strike]] or otherwise speedy enemy units, where his Knockback is pretty much guaranteed to gain them more ground.

==Strategy==
Because of his 100% chance to knockback, units with 350+ range are basically required unless it is a [[:Category:Rusher-class Cats|rusher]]. Pile up ranged Cats such as [[Gross Cat (Normal Cat)|Macho Leg Cat]] or [[Lizard Cat (Normal Cat)|King Dragon Cat]] while spamming [[:Category:Meatshield-class Cats|meatshields]] ([[Cat (Normal Cat)|Mohawk Cat]], [[Crazed Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Crazed Macho Cat]], [[Tank Cat (Normal Cat)|Eraser Cat]], etc.). [[Salon Cat (Rare Cat)|Paris Cat]] and [[Figure Skating Cats (Super Rare Cat)|Drama Cats]] are especially good against him, since they have Area Attack. If spawned in groups, it's recommended to use the default [[Cat Cannon]] to sync them up and reduce their pushing power.

Out of all the "big units" you could throw out against a pack of H. Nahs, one of the best choices is someone any player can recruit two chapters after H. Nah's debut stage: [[Ururun Wolf (Special Cat)|Ururun Wolf]]. With a knockback effect of her own, she has a chance to sync up the H. Nahs every time she attacks, and she attacks quite often while outranging them. [[:Category:Tanker-class Cats|Tanky]] [[:Category:Cats with Knockback Immunity|Knockback-immune Cats]] can also be useful against H. Nah, such as [[Sodom (Uber Rare Cat)|God-Emperor Sodom]] or [[Kai (Uber Rare Cat)|Divine Kai μ]], if they can also outrange H. Nah then they will be much more helpful. Units with long backswing and no time between attacks have a rebound attack which will also work in favor with H. Nah's knockback, but if they don't then that is fine too. Some examples are [[Express Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Maglev Cat]], [[Bahamut Cat (Special Cat)|Awakened Bahamut Cat]] and [[Sanada Yukimura (Uber Rare Cat)|Yukimura]] although this is less viable later on in the game where buffs can escalate his damage to the point where he kills most rusher units outright or inflicts enough damage to stagger the unit.

